    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30103" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">muscŭlōsus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		musculus. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Muscular, fleshy</i> (post-Aug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cor naturā musculosum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cels. 4,
					1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pectora,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col. 8,
					2</span></i>
			. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Musclōsus</span></b> , for
				Musculosus, <i>a Roman surname</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Inscr. Grut. 337</span></i>.</div>
